REASON
AutoWriter had no example. Unlike the other example pages in this repository, which are
deliberately plain because they demonstrate structural behaviour (modal stacking, form
control wiring), this component's entire output is a visual effect — a demo that does not
look good does not demonstrate it. The page is therefore designed rather than merely
functional: a dark editorial/terminal treatment, a hero whose headline types itself, and
one accent colour per demo so several writers running at once stay legible.

Structure, each section demonstrating something the guide states:

  Hero          headline typed on load, ending in '~1200~' so the caret is left blinking;
                a subject line that cycles words through one recursive writeText() call,
                each cycle being "word + hold + backspace exactly the word's length" —
                the pattern the guide recommends over looping in code, because the erase
                stays in step with the typing.
  Playground    the script in an editable textarea against live controls for every config
                property, plus Run / stop() / deleteText(5) / Clear, a status line, and a
                generated code snippet. Four presets: Basic, Rewrite (type, pause,
                backspace 14, finish differently), Multi-line, Boot log.
  Directives    '|', '*n*' and '~n~' in three cards, each with its OWN writer and target,
                since two writers must never share an element.
  Sequence      one NodeList and one array through a single writeText() call, typed in
                order with the callback firing once at the end.
  Bad input     five buttons whose calls all throw synchronously, printing the real Error
                message. This is the section that shows validation happens at the call,
                not inside a timer.

Two consumer-side techniques the README calls out because the library cannot do them for
you: giving '.vAutoWriterBlinker' a display and height (the library styles it with a left
border only, leaving its size at the mercy of the surrounding line), and reserving a
min-height on every target so the page does not shift as text arrives.

The page uses system font stacks and no external assets, so it works offline behind
`python3 -m http.server` like the other examples. It follows the loading contract:
data-id="vUX" and data-library-root="../../", which processAssetPath() strips to
"../../assets/".

VERIFICATION
Every string the page types was run through the real module in the harness: the four
presets, the hero line, the five cycling words, the three directive demos and the
collection-mode call all produce their intended output, and all five "bad input" calls
throw. 30 assertions, all passing. One defect was found this way and fixed before
shipping: the Boot log preset read "autoWriter.css~500~ok", which renders as
"autoWriter.cssok" — corrected to "autoWriter.css...~500~ok".
Every id and data-attribute selector in main.js was cross-checked against index.html (23
ids, 4 presets, 5 error buttons, 3 directive demos — no misses), and every asset the page
requests was confirmed to return 200 over `python3 -m http.server` from the repository
root.
